error: `receive` on a connection holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_net_blocking_in_async.sg:3:17
 3 |     return conn.receive(ref buffer)
   |                 ^^^^^^^
  hint: `await conn.receiveAsync(ref buffer)` does the same work without holding the thread
